\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Bounds on the input potential}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{Use #{p,r,s,W_j(\cdot;s),\mathcal P_j} of the
\vocabk{normalized marginal map}{fdip-01DJ}.
Choose #{a>0} with #{6a<1/8} and #{6a/r^2<1/(8s)}, and
fix #{M,B>0}. For an even #{C^2} function #{R}, define
##{\lVert R\rVert_{a,4,2}=
\max_{j=0,1,2}\sup_{x\in\RR}
\frac{\ue^{-ax^2}|R^{(j)}(x)|}{1+|x|^{4-j}}.}
For any function #{f}, define the weaker function norm
##{\lVert f\rVert_*=\sup_{y\in\RR}
\frac{\ue^{-y^2/(4s)}|f(y)|}{1+|y|^6}.}
For #{0<h\le g_*}, the \newvocab{controlled input domain}
#{\mathcal D(h,g_*)} consists of even #{C^2} potentials
##{V=hW_4(\cdot;s)+\nu W_2(\cdot;s)+R}
satisfying all of
##{\begin{gathered}
\mathcal P_0R=\mathcal P_2R=\mathcal P_4R=0,\qquad
|\nu|\le Mh^2,\qquad \lVert R\rVert_{a,4,2}\le Mh^2,\\
\inf_{x\in\RR}V(x)>-\infty,\qquad
V''(x)\ge -Bh,\qquad |V''(x)|\le Bg_*(1+x^2)
\quad(x\in\RR).
\end{gathered}}
The derivative and curvature bounds are separate requirements.
The norm #{\lVert\cdot\rVert_*} will measure an output remainder;
it is not part of the definition of #{\mathcal D(h,g_*)}.}
